%SIXMD 1
# @?XARGS - BUILD COMMAND INVOCATIONS FROM TEXT RECORDS

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-N NUMBER - LIMIT ARGUMENTS PER INVOCATION
RUN THE COMMAND WHEN THE BOUNDED ARGUMENT VECTOR REACHES NUMBER ARGUMENTS.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?[COMMAND]
COMMAND TO RUN.  ECHO IS USED WHEN COMMAND IS OMITTED.

### @?[ARG...]
INITIAL ARGUMENTS PREPENDED TO EACH INVOCATION.

## DESCRIPTION

XARGS READS S6REC TEXT FROM STANDARD INPUT, SPLITS RECORDS ON SPACE OR TAB,
PACKS EACH TOKEN AS A NATIVE COUNTED SIXBIT ARGUMENT, AND RUNS COMMAND THROUGH
THE CURRENT RUN V2 ABI.  EXPORTED ENVIRONMENT AND STANDARD DESCRIPTORS ARE
INHERITED BY THE CHILD.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - ALL INVOCATIONS SUCCEEDED
### @?1 - INPUT OR CHILD COMMAND FAILED
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE
### @?126 - COMMAND COULD NOT BE LAUNCHED
### @?127 - COMMAND WAS NOT FOUND

